# Taplink SDK – Best Practices

---

## 1. Lifecycle Management

### SDK initialization — Application level (once)
```kotlin
class MyApplication : Application() {
    override fun onCreate() {
        super.onCreate()
        TaplinkSDK.init(this, TaplinkConfig(
            appId = BuildConfig.TAPLINK_APP_ID,
            merchantId = BuildConfig.TAPLINK_MERCHANT_ID,
            secretKey = BuildConfig.TAPLINK_SECRET_KEY
        ))
    }
}
```

### Connection — Activity/Service level
```kotlin
class MainActivity : AppCompatActivity() {

    override fun onCreate(savedInstanceState: Bundle?) {
        super.onCreate(savedInstanceState)
        // Register persistent status listener
        TaplinkSDK.setConnectionListener(connectionStatusListener)
    }

    override fun onResume() {
        super.onResume()
        if (!TaplinkSDK.isConnected()) {
            TaplinkSDK.connect(connectionConfig, oneTimeConnectListener)
        }
    }

    override fun onDestroy() {
        super.onDestroy()
        TaplinkSDK.removeConnectionListener()  // Always remove to avoid memory leaks
        TaplinkSDK.disconnect()
    }
}
```

> **Rule:** Always call `removeConnectionListener()` and `disconnect()` in `onDestroy()`.

---

## 2. Two Types of Connection Listeners

| Method | Purpose | Lifecycle |
|--------|---------|-----------|
| `TaplinkSDK.connect(config, listener)` | Notified for this specific connect call only | One-shot |
| `TaplinkSDK.setConnectionListener(listener)` | Notified for all future status changes | Persistent |

**Use both:**
- `connect()` listener → react to initial connection result
- `setConnectionListener()` → monitor ongoing status (disconnects, reconnects, errors)

```kotlin
// Persistent observer — set in onCreate()
TaplinkSDK.setConnectionListener(object : ConnectionListener {
    override fun onConnected(deviceId: String, taproVersion: String) {
        runOnUiThread { enablePaymentButton(true) }
    }
    override fun onDisconnected(reason: String) {
        runOnUiThread { enablePaymentButton(false) }
    }
    override fun onError(error: ConnectionError) {
        runOnUiThread { showConnectionError(error.message) }
    }
})
```

