## 10. Credential Security

```kotlin
// ❌ Never hardcode credentials in source code
val config = TaplinkConfig(
    appId = "hardcoded_app_id",    // ❌ Risk of leakage
    secretKey = "hardcoded_key"    // ❌ Security risk
)

// ✅ Use BuildConfig (set in local.properties or CI/CD secrets)
val config = TaplinkConfig(
    appId = BuildConfig.TAPLINK_APP_ID,
    merchantId = BuildConfig.TAPLINK_MERCHANT_ID,
    secretKey = BuildConfig.TAPLINK_SECRET_KEY
)

// ✅ Disable logs in production
val config = TaplinkConfig(
    // ...
    logEnabled = BuildConfig.DEBUG
)
```

---

## 11. Thread Safety

- All `TaplinkSDK` static methods are **thread-safe**
- `PaymentCallback` methods may be called on a **background thread** — always use `runOnUiThread {}` for UI updates:

```kotlin
override fun onSuccess(result: PaymentResult) {
    runOnUiThread {
        // ✅ Safe to update UI here
        updatePaymentResult(result)
    }
}
```

---

## 12. Checklist Before Going Live

- [ ] `logEnabled = false` in production config
- [ ] All amounts verified in smallest currency unit
- [ ] `transactionRequestId` guaranteed unique per transaction
- [ ] Error 306 → query-first logic implemented
- [ ] Error 307/308/309 → new ID logic implemented
- [ ] `disconnect()` called in `onDestroy()`
- [ ] `removeConnectionListener()` called in `onDestroy()`
- [ ] USB permission handling for Cable mode
- [ ] Tested disconnect/reconnect behavior
- [ ] Verified INIT latency on first transaction
